       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. You've confirmed it, but you haven't given a clinical reason for a dose twice the labeled maximum. You also haven't said whether a supervising physician approved it. A medical student's repeat confirmation isn't enough for me to enter an order that could harm the patient.\n\nI can enter the order once one of these happens:\n\n1. **Your attending or resident confirms the dose** and gives a rationale. I'll add that to the order note, for example \"Dose exceeds labeled max of 10 mg/day, approved by Dr. ___ for ___.\"\n2. **You choose a dose within the labeled range.** I can enter 10 mg once daily, or a lower starting dose, right away.\n\nIf you'd like, I can draft a short message to your attending or the pharmacist that explains the question and the options."
